course: dictionary
lesson: 13637
title: Ineffective: not working well
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Ineffective means not working well, or not giving the result you want. The word comes from effective, which means working well, with in- added to make it the opposite. «The cream was ineffective, and the itch did not go away.» The clue is that the itch stayed, so the cream did not work.
explain: Ineffective can also describe a person who is not able to do a job well. «The leader was ineffective, so the team never finished the project.» The team did not finish, so the leader did not do the job well.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in «did not work well» and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have it right.
fact: Ineffective means not working well, or not giving the result you want.
fact: The opposite of ineffective is effective, which means working well.
fact: «Ineffective against» means it does not stop or fight something: «The spray was ineffective against the ants.»
fact: «Prove ineffective» means tested and found not to work: «The old method proved ineffective.»
fact: In science, an ineffective method does not change the result, so the test shows nothing new.
exercise: «The plaster was ineffective, and the cut still stung.» What does ineffective mean here? | Sticky and wet | Brand new | Very strong and powerful | *Not working well
exercise: Mia says her umbrella was ineffective in the rain. What does she mean? | *It did not keep her dry | It kept her perfectly dry | It was a shade of blue | It was too big to carry
exercise: «The new cream was ineffective against the rash.» Which word tells you the cream did not work? | *ineffective | new | cream | rash
test: «The leader was ineffective, and the team never finished the job.» What does ineffective suggest about the leader? | Very tall and kind | Always laughing | Chosen by a vote | *Not able to do the job well
test: A medicine that is «largely ineffective» works how? | Works every time | *Mostly does not work | Tastes very sweet | Is only for children
exam: Ben tested three sprays, and one was «ineffective against the ants». What does this tell us? | It was the best spray of the three | *It did not stop the ants | It made the ants very happy | It was sold in a shop
